    "notes": [
      "Register. Spoken Tang Chinese is only indirectly documented. Lines marked 'vern' use words and constructions attested in Tang-era colloquial sources: Dunhuang bianwen and letter manuals (書儀), Wang Fanzhi and Hanshan poems, You xian ku, Tang tales, Bai Juyi's plain-style poems, and the Chan records. Everything else ('wenyan') is short, plain literary Chinese of the kind a Tang speaker could plausibly say. 'constructed' in src means the wording is composed, not quoted.",
      "Colloquial items used: 阿誰 / 甚人 'who', 何物 'what', 你 (2nd person, Tang), 渠 / 伊 (3rd person), 莫 'don't', 爭 'how', 喫 'eat/drink', 將…來/將去 'bring/take', V殺 (intensifier: 熱殺人), 子細 'careful', 好在 (greeting), 好去 / 好住 (farewell to one leaving / staying), 不審 (respectful greeting), 珍重 (leave-taking), 起居 (salutation), sentence-final 無 as a question (能飲一杯無, 白居易), 也 / 矣 as sentence finals, 纔 'only', 真箇 'really'. Address terms: 郎君, 娘子, 阿郎, 阿婆, 阿娘, 阿耶, 阿兄, 大德 (to monks), 檀越 (to patrons), 博士 (tea server, 封氏聞見記), 措大 (poor scholar), 田舍漢 (bumpkin), birth-order names like 三郎, 十二郎, 白二十二.",
      "Avoided as too late or modern: aspect 了 and 着; plural 們; 的 as possessive (none used); 這/那 as everyday demonstratives (used only in Chan quotations, otherwise 此); 什麼 (late Tang and Five Dynasties: only Chan 作麼生 is used, marked as slightly risky), 便宜 'cheap' (in Tang it meant 'convenient'), 乾杯, 救命, 小心 as a warning, 慢走, 行行好, 借過. Also no carp sold (鯉 taboo under Tang law, 酉陽雜俎 卷17) and no 宮市 complaints (abolished in 805). Grapes are written 蒲萄 (Tang spelling; 葡 is also missing from the dictionary).",
      "815 content: the assassination of 武元衡 (6th month, 3rd day; 靖安坊), 裴度 wounded and saved by his felt hat (舊唐書 裴度傳), the great search of the city, the 10,000-string reward, Jinwu escorts for ministers (資治通鑑 卷239), the 淮西 war and 李光顏's victories, suspicion of 恆州 (王承宗), 白居易's memorial and his demotion (7th/8th month, so slightly ahead of an early-6th-month start), 元和 deflation (錢重物輕, 短陌 strings, 惡錢 bad coins), and the summer study season (槐花黃，舉子忙; 夏課). Guard lines quote 唐律疏議: curfew 笞二十, passes 公驗/文牒, the ward wall 杖七十, private forbidden arms 徒一年半, and killing a night intruder 勿論.",
      "Readings. bax is authoritative: one Baxter syllable per hanzi, chosen by meaning from tts2/mc_dict.json, not the dictionary's first reading (for example 好 xawX 'good', 少 syewX/syewH 'few'/'young', 相 sjangH in 相公/宰相 but sjang in 相見, 上 dzyangX 'submit' in 上疏, 否 pjuwX as a question particle, 請 tshjengX, 出 tsyhwit, 乾 kan 'dry', 能 nong, 一切 tshejH, 人參 srim, 坊 pjang, 禁 kimH, 宿 sjuwk, 索 srjaek 'search', 量 ljangH 'measure (noun)', 將雨 hjuH (verb), 過 kwa 'pass by' / kwaH 'fault'). zhm repeats zh with 字[bax] on every polyphonic character, for tts2 MC.parse and tts2/index.html.",
      "Uncertain readings: 金吾 吾 (ngu here; some commentators read it as 禦 ngjoX 'to guard'); 甚 'what/very' (dzyimX; the dictionary also gives dzyimH); 繚綾 繚 (lewX; lew is also possible); 撞 (draewng; draewngH is also listed); 壽 in 福壽 (dzyuwX; dzyuwH is also possible); 看 (khan; Tang verse uses both tones); 從 in 衛從 (dzjowngH 'retinue'); 減 (heamX; keamX is also listed)."
    ],
